From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:52:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Clear EAPOL portValid when a WPA STA reassociates

When a WPA STA associates again while hostapd keeps its EAPOL state
machine, portValid keeps the value true from the previous 4-way
handshake. The authenticator PAE state machine then authorizes the
port before the new 4-way handshake installs a pairwise key. This
happens when EAP succeeds, or at once with PMKSA caching. If the AP
removed the STA from the driver for the new association, the new
driver entry is authorized and has no key. In an IEEE 802.11be build,
a new Authentication frame also replaces the WPA state machine, unless
the STA uses PMF and is authorized. The new machine clears portValid,
but keyDone stays set, so a reassociation with PMKSA caching enters
HELD and the AP disconnects the STA.

Clear portValid and keyDone for the new association, because a new
state machine starts with both flags clear. The PTKINITDONE state of
the WPA authenticator validates the port again, so the port is
authorized after the new key is in place. With keyDone clear, the
PMKSA caching path waits for PTKINITDONE and does not enter HELD. No
state machine step runs between the clear and the reauthentication
request or the PMKSA caching state. In AUTHENTICATED state, a step
with portValid clear and no reauthentication request reports a
disconnection.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/ieee802_1x.c |   14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_1x.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_1x.c
@@ -1481,6 +1481,20 @@ void ieee802_1x_new_station(struct hosta
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_FILS */
 
+	if (reassoc && hapd->conf->wpa) {
+		/*
+		 * The port of the new association is valid only after its
+		 * 4-way handshake. No state machine step may run between this
+		 * clear and the reauthentication request or the PMKSA caching
+		 * state below: in AUTHENTICATED state, such a step reports a
+		 * disconnection. Clear keyDone too, because the PMKSA caching
+		 * path does not enter AUTHENTICATING, and an old keyDone with
+		 * portValid false moves it to HELD.
+		 */
+		sta->eapol_sm->portValid = false;
+		sta->eapol_sm->keyDone = false;
+	}
+
 	pmksa = wpa_auth_sta_get_pmksa(sta->wpa_sm);
 	if (pmksa) {
 		hostapd_logger(hapd, sta->addr, HOSTAPD_MODULE_IEEE8021X,
